# Security review before commit

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L0 gate.

## Use This When

- A commit is about to be made.

## Stop Here If

- Every item below was checked for the staged change.

## Core rule

- No secrets, tokens, passwords or personal data in tracked files, fixtures or seed data; generated test data uses `@example.test` addresses.
- Every table defines `PERMISSIONS`; a table without them is closed (`NONE`) until a reason to open it exists. Field-level secrets (password hashes) are hidden from `select`.
- Server-only tables are marked `-- @replicate none` and never reach a client replica.
- Queries never concatenate input into SurrealQL; values travel as parameters of declared shapes and commands.
- Input from outside the trusted core is parsed with Zod before use.
- New dependencies are pinned in the root catalog and come from a known publisher.
